# List 3 – Sales and Marketing
- bargain : a good deal; an advantageous purchase (noun) | At 40% off, this laptop is a real ___ for students.
- black market : illegal trading of goods that are not allowed to be sold, or that are too scarce for everyone who wants them | During the shortage, baby formula was sold on the ___ at three times its normal price.
- brand awareness : the extent to which potential customers recognize a brand and correctly associate it with a product; the main goal of advertising in a product's early years | Our first-year campaign aims to build ___ before we focus on sales.
- end users : the final consumers of a product or service, at the end of the distribution channel (not necessarily the people who buy or order it) | The hospital buys the software, but the ___ are the nurses who use it every day.
- generic products : goods sold under the name of their product type instead of a brand name, lightly marketed and competing mainly on price | Many shoppers switch to ___ such as store-brand pasta when prices rise.
- make : the name of the company that manufactures a product, especially a car (noun) | "Which ___ is your car?" "It's a Toyota."
- penetrate a market : to succeed in entering a particular market | Lululemon used yoga studios to ___ that had long been dominated by Nike.
- raw materials : materials such as oil, cotton or sugar cane in their natural state, before they are processed | Rising prices for ___ like cocoa have pushed Ferrero to raise its prices.
- stiff competition : competition that is more severe than usual | Cirque du Soleil faces ___ from streaming platforms for families' entertainment budgets.
- vendor : a person or company that sells something | The IT department chose a new ___ for its cloud services after three demos.
- make a killing : (idiom, avoid in business writing) to make an enormous profit; to become an enormous success | Investors who bought the shares early were able to ___ when the company went public.
- talk someone into something : (idiom, avoid in business writing) to persuade or convince someone; to win someone over | A good salesperson knows how to ___ without sounding pushy.
